@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "customer.portal"

Feature: Project Details Source Code Access
	Testing the Source Code Access feature for the Project Details portlet.

Setup:
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pjd.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PJD                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pjd.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PJD                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pjd.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PJD                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                          |
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Name   | Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| Code   | ZENPARZENPAR                  | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" on the account "Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Partner Manager |
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName}" assigned to the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Assigned Team Nested Field | ${staticAssignedTeamNestedField} | |
	| Code                       | PJDZENPJDZEN                     | |
	| Name                       | Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}    | |
	| Region                     | United States                    | |
	| Status                     | Active                           | |
	| Tier                       | T1                               | |
	* I assign the team with the name "Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	* I assign the team with the name "Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Watcher |
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code   | DUPZENDUPZEN                     | |
	| Name   | Dupzen - ${staticProjectName}    | |
	| Region | United States                    | |
	| Status | Active                           | |
	| Tier   | T1                               | |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Dupzen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Dupzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| ZENPARZENPAR |
	| PJDZENPJDZEN |
	| DUPZENDUPZEN |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| ZENPARZENPAR |
	| PJDZENPJDZEN |
	| DUPZENDUPZEN |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Dupzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Zenpar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Dupzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I automatically have all non Source Code Access users removed from the GitHub repository 

Scenario: View source code access user
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	New source code access users on an approved project should be able to gain access to the proper GitHub repository.

	Given I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "PJDZENPJDZEN" should be part of the support site
	When I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I go to the Project Details page 
	And I search for the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Source Code Access tab
	And I add a Source Code Access user with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	Then the Source Code Access user panel for a user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" should be visible with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	And the Source Code Access user details for a user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" should be visible with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	When I wait for "30" seconds
	And I accept the GitHub repository invitation using the username "infoservicesqa" and the password "rejoicealways123"
	Then I should be able to view the is-support-integration repository using the username "infoservicesqa" and the password "rejoicealways123"

Scenario: View source code access user added to closed project
	New source code access users on a closed project should be able to gain access to the proper GitHub repository after project approval.

	Given I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the support organization with the code "PJDZENPJDZEN" should be part of the support site
	When I update a koroneiki account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" to have the following values
	| Status | Closed | |
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I go to the Project Details page 
	And I search for the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Source Code Access tab
	And I add a Source Code Access user with the following values on a closed project
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	Then the Source Code Access user panel for a user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" should be visible with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	And the Source Code Access user details for a user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" should be visible with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	When I wait for "30" seconds
	Then I should not be able to view the GitHub repository invitation using the username "infoservicesqa" and the password "rejoicealways123"
	And I should not be able to view the is-support-integration repository using the username "infoservicesqa" and the password "rejoicealways123"

Scenario: View source code access user added to expired project
	New source code access users on an expired project should not be able to gain access to the proper GitHub repository.

	Given I generate past static start and end dates
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Quantity                | 1                            | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Platinum Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                        | |
	| Quantity                | 1                            | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                     | |
	And I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I go to the Project Details page 
	And I search for the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the project with the name "Pjdzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I go to the Source Code Access tab
	And I add a Source Code Access user with the following values on a closed project
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	Then the Source Code Access user panel for a user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" should be visible with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	And the Source Code Access user details for a user with the email address "info.services.qa@gmail.com" should be visible with the following values
	| Name            | Info Services QA           |
	| Email Address   | info.services.qa@gmail.com |
	| GitHub Username | infoservicesqa             |
	When I wait for "30" seconds
	Then I should not be able to view the GitHub repository invitation using the username "infoservicesqa" and the password "rejoicealways123"
	And I should not be able to view the is-support-integration repository using the username "infoservicesqa" and the password "rejoicealways123"

